(22, NULL, 'Akagera Sacco Kayonza (ASK)', 'logos/img_6a60dac43eae8.png', 17, 'Motorcycle Driver', 'motorcycle-driver', 'Akagera Sacco Kayonza (ASK) is a District Savings and Credit Cooperative (D-SACCO) established following the consolidation of Tuelve Umurenge Sacco’s operating within Kayonza District, in accordance with the Government of Rwanda SACCO consolidation framework. ASK is duly registered under RCA Certificate No. N° RGDG013385 and licensed by the National Bank of Rwanda (BNR).\r\nIn accordance with Law N° 072/2021 of 05/11/2021 governing Deposit-Taking Microfinance Institutions, ASK is authorized to carry out microfinance activities in the Republic of Rwanda.\r\nTo achieve its mission and strengthen institutional efficiency, ASK is looking for a qualified, competent, committed, proactive, and self-motivated individual to fill the following vacant position:\r\nJOB ADVERT- MOTORCYCLE DRIVER\r\nTo achieve its mission and strengthen institutional efficiency, ASK is seeking to recruit a competent, committed, professional, and self-motivated Motorcycle Driver to join the institution.', 'Under the supervision and guidance of the Logistics Officer, the Motorcycle Driver shall perform the following duties and responsibilities:\r\nTo work diligently on the assigned work on time and to produce results;\r\nTo comply with the instructions of the employer or his/her representative;\r\nTo comply with the laws, regulations and decisions of the Cooperative;\r\nTo take good care of and manage the equipment assigned to him/her in his/her work;\r\nTo be at work and to respect working days and hours;\r\nTo maintain confidentiality of work;\r\nTo follow the principles and rules governing the conduct of the Cooperative\'s business activities;\r\nSafely transport staff, official documents, and authorized items to designated locations. \r\nDeliver and collect official correspondence, banking documents, and other materials within the required timelines. \r\nEnsure the confidentiality and security of documents and items carried on behalf of the SACCO. \r\nConduct daily inspections of the motorcycle, including fuel, oil, tires, brakes, lights, and other safety components. \r\nKeep the motorcycle clean, roadworthy, and in good working condition. \r\nReport mechanical faults or accidents immediately and arrange maintenance as directed. \r\nMaintain accurate records of trips, mileage, fuel consumption, maintenance, and repairs. \r\nEnsure that the motorcycle has valid insurance, registration, inspection certificates, and other required documents. \r\nStrictly comply with Rwanda traffic laws and road safety regulations. \r\nWear the required protective gear and ensure any passenger uses appropriate safety equipment. \r\nSupport branch operations by running official errands, including delivering mail, collecting supplies \r\nAssist in transporting promotional materials and supporting outreach activities, member mobilization, and financial literacy campaigns. \r\nMaintain confidentiality of member information and all SACCO business encountered during duties. \r\nReport any security risks, road incidents, or suspicious activities encountered during assignments. \r\nEnsure efficient fuel usage and prevent misuse of the motorcycle or other organizational resources. \r\nBe available for official assignments within the SACCO\'s operational area as directed by management. \r\nPerform any other duties assigned by the authorized supervisor that are consistent with the position.', 'Minimum Advanced Level (A2) in any field. \r\nValid Category A Motorcycle Driving License. \r\nAt least 2 years\' experience as a motorcycle rider/driver. \r\nGood knowledge of Kayonza District and surrounding areas. \r\nClean driving record. \r\n Basic knowledge of motorcycle maintenance.\r\nIntegrity and trustworthiness. \r\nTime management. \r\nGood communication skills. \r\nCustomer service orientation. \r\nAbility to work under pressure. \r\nReliability and punctuality. \r\nPhysical fitness', 'Required Application Documents\r\nApplicants must submit the following documents:\r\nMotivation letter addressed to the Chairperson of the Board of Directors.\r\nUpdated Curriculum Vitae (CV) with at least three (3) professional referees and their contact details.\r\nCopy of academic Certificate and Driving license.\r\nCopy of National ID.\r\nCertificates of service rendered or previous employment certificates proving relevant experience.\r\nAny other relevant supporting documents proving experience and competencies.', '', 'Applications must be submitted in soft copy as one single combined PDF document to their email address, \r\nThe subject of the email must clearly indicate the position applied for: “Application for Motorcycle Driver.”\r\nDeadline for submission: 24th July, 2026, at 5:00 PM.\r\nLate applications will not be accepted.\r\nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted for the next stage of the recruitment process.\r\nAdditional Information\r\nASK promotes equal opportunity. All Qualified candidates are encouraged to apply.\r\nNo fees or any form of compensation shall be requested at any stage of the recruitment process.\r\nBenefits are competitive and aligned with those offered by other financial institutions.', '', 'ask.recruitment26@gmail.com', 'Eastern', 'Kayonza', 'Mukarange', 'Full-time', '1 to 3 years', 'Minimum Advanced Level (A2) in any field', 'RWF', 'monthly', '2026-07-24', 0, 'archived', 302, 0, 1, '2026-07-22 14:59:16', '2026-07-24 15:23:54', NULL),
(23, NULL, 'COOPEC IKIRENGA', 'logos/img_6a60e5177bc48.jpeg', 15, 'Teller', 'teller-1784734999', 'COOPEC IKIRENGA is a Financial Service Cooperative operating in the Northern Province of Rwanda supervised by National Bank of Rwanda. Its creation is a result of merger of five SACCOs (COOPEC ITI, COOPEC CODEMARU, CSTCR SACCO, CSPKI and TRASO) that decided to form one single entity named “COOPEC IKIRENGA” in May, 2024 while the existing SACCOs remained as its branches. COOPEC IKIRENGA headquarter is located in Rulindo district, Base Sector, Rwamahwa Cell, Base Village. \r\nIt is from that background that the Management of COOPEC IKIRENGAinforms the public that it is recruiting competent and qualified staff.', 'Key ResponsibilitiesUnder the supervision and guidance of the Branch Operations Officer/Outlet responsible:\r\n\r\nConducts cash related services for customers/ members, e.g., withdrawals and deposits.\r\nInitiates transfers from customer/member accounts, e.g., interbranch transfer.\r\nPerforms check-related services for customers/ members, e.g., crediting a cheque.\r\nSupports in day closure.\r\nSupports in opening, filling, discharging, and closing a till.\r\nPerforms cross-selling.\r\nPerform any other tasks requested by the Branch Operations Officer/Outlet responsible.Education & Experiences Required', 'At least secondary education (A2) in Accounting, have a Bachelor Degree in Business Management, Finance, Accounting, Business Administration Economics or Related Field is a preferred Added Advantage.\r\nBasic IT literacy of CBS and Microsoft Office. \r\nAbility to handle transactions accurately and responsibly.\r\nGood math skills.\r\nAttention to detail.\r\nCustomer satisfaction oriented.', 'To be Rwandan\r\nAge limit: 30 Years\r\nNot to have been sentenced to a term of imprisonment equal to or exceeding six (6) months.\r\nNot to have been dismissed from any other institution unless applicant is entitled to reinstatement under laws and regulations in force.\r\nNot have been involved in the bankruptcy of a financial institution\r\n\r\nRequired documents for application:\r\nAn application letter addressed to the Chairperson of the BoD of COOPEC IKIRENGA.\r\nA detailed/updated curriculum vitae.\r\nCopy of academic degree and Certificate where Required.\r\nA proof of work experience if any.\r\nA photocopy of the Identity card.\r\nFull addresses of three referees with recommendations letter, including preferably one of previous supervisors.', '', 'Interested and qualified candidates must submit their applications from their own email addresses to recruitment@coopecikirenga.rw . Applications submitted using another person\'s email address will not be considered.\r\nApplication Deadline is the 31st July, 2026. \r\nOnly a single document (PDF Format) will be considered\r\nNB: E-mail subject should be the Applicant Names followed by a Position is applying for.\r\n\r\nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted for the next stage of the recruitment process.', '', 'recruitment@coopecikirenga.rw', 'Northern', 'RULINDO', 'rulindo', 'Full-time', '', 'Bachelor&#039;s Degree', 'RWF', 'monthly', '2026-07-31', 1, 'published', 25, 0, 1, '2026-07-22 15:43:19', '2026-07-27 05:49:34', NULL),
(24, NULL, 'Impactful Solutions Rwanda (ISR-CBC)', 'logos/img_6a61116d73f5d.png', 11, 'School Principal – SOS Kayonza School', 'school-principal-sos-kayonza-school', 'About Impactful Solutions Rwanda (ISR-CBC)\r\nImpactful Solutions Rwanda (ISR-CBC) is a registered social business established by SOS Children\'s Villages Rwanda to manage and operate its income-generating and service delivery enterprises, including schools, a training center, guest houses, bakery, farms and events management services. Established in December 2025 and headquartered in Kacyiru, Gasabo District, Kigali, ISR-CBC is committed to operational excellence, financial sustainability and creating lasting social impact.\r\nAs the social business company responsible for managing SOS Children\'s Villages Rwanda schools, ISR-CBC is guided by the vision \"Where Children Thrive and Communities Rise.\" The organization is dedicated to delivering quality, inclusive and sustainable education that equips children and young people with the knowledge, skills, values and competencies needed to thrive in an ever-changing world.\r\nISR-CBC empowers communities through education, skills development, entrepreneurship and innovative social business solutions that promote self-reliance, economic opportunity and sustainable community development.\r\nSOS Kayonza School is a comprehensive institution offering Kindergarten, Primary Education, Lower Secondary Education (Ordinary Level), TVET Short Courses (Tailoring, Carpentry, Welding and Hairdressing), together with Day and Boarding Services. To strengthen the school\'s continued growth and transformation, ISR-CBC is seeking an experienced, visionary and results-oriented professional to serve as School Principal.\r\nJob Purpose\r\nThe School Principal is the chief executive and instructional leader of SOS Kayonza School and is responsible for providing strategic leadership, ensuring academic excellence, strengthening English as the primary language of communication and instruction, expanding TVET opportunities, ensuring compliance with MINEDUC, NESA and other regulatory requirements and driving the long-term growth and sustainability of the school.\r\nThe School Principal will cultivate a high-performance culture that delivers outstanding learner outcomes, develops staff capability, promotes innovation, strengthens stakeholder confidence, improves financial sustainability, and positions SOS Kayonza School among Rwanda\'s leading centers of educational excellence.', '1. Strategic Leadership and School Improvement\r\nProvide visionary leadership and implement the School Improvement Plan aligned with organizational and national education priorities.\r\nPromote a culture of excellence, accountability, innovation, discipline and continuous improvement.\r\nLead strategic planning, institutional performance monitoring and evidence-based decision-making.\r\nPosition SOS Kayonza School among the top-performing schools in Rwanda.\r\n2. Academic Leadership and Learner Achievement\r\nEnsure effective implementation of the Competency-Based Curriculum across Kindergarten, Primary, Secondary and TVET programs.\r\nMonitor learner performance and implement interventions to improve academic outcomes.\r\nConduct classroom observations, instructional coaching and academic reviews.\r\nPromote literacy, numeracy, digital learning, critical thinking and problem-solving skills.\r\n3. English Language Excellence\r\nEstablish English as the primary language of communication and instruction throughout the school.\r\nImplement English language improvement programs for learners and staff.\r\nPromote an English-speaking culture through assemblies, debates, public speaking, reading programs and staff development.\r\n4. TVET Development and Innovation\r\nStrengthen existing TVET programs and introduce new market-driven technical courses.\r\nBuild partnerships with industries, employers and training institutions.\r\nPromote entrepreneurship, internships, apprenticeships and graduate employability.\r\nEnsure all TVET programs comply with national quality and certification standards.\r\n5. Quality Assurance and Compliance\r\nEnsure full compliance with MINEDUC, NESA and other regulatory requirements.\r\nCoordinate school inspection readiness and implement recommendations from inspections and audits.\r\nMaintain high standards of governance, quality assurance, safeguarding and risk management.\r\n6. Student Welfare and Boarding Management\r\nEnsure a safe, inclusive and child-friendly learning environment.\r\nOversee boarding facilities and student welfare services.\r\nPromote child safeguarding, positive discipline, leadership development and psychosocial well-being.\r\n7. Human Resource Leadership\r\nSupport recruitment, supervision, mentorship and development of teaching and support staff.\r\nImplement a performance management system with measurable annual targets.\r\nPromote continuous professional development and teamwork.\r\n8. Community and Stakeholder Engagement\r\nBuild productive relationships with parents, local authorities, development partners, industries and the wider community.\r\nRepresent the school professionally in all external engagements.\r\nPromote the school\'s reputation and strengthen stakeholder confidence.\r\n9. Financial Sustainability and Resource Management\r\nPrepare and manage the school\'s annual budget.\r\nLead initiatives that increase student enrolment and improve boarding occupancy.\r\nIncrease internally generated revenue through program expansion, strategic partnerships, facility utilization and approved income-generating initiatives.\r\nImplement cost-efficiency measures while maintaining educational quality and student welfare.\r\nEnsure transparent financial management, prudent resource utilization and long-term institutional sustainability.', 'Minimum Qualifications\r\n\r\nApplicants should possess:\r\n\r\nA master’s degree in educational leadership, Educational Management, School Administration, Curriculum Studies or another related education field.\r\nOR\r\n\r\nA bachelor’s degree in education or a related field with a minimum of three (3) years of relevant educational leadership experience.\r\nProfessional training in Educational Leadership will be an added advantage.\r\n\r\nAdditional certification in Leadership, Quality Assurance, TVET Management or School Improvement will be an added advantage.\r\n\r\nExperience\r\n\r\nApplicants must demonstrate:\r\n\r\n3–5 years of progressive educational leadership experience.\r\nProven success in improving academic outcomes and institutional performance.\r\nExperience managing multi-level schools comprising Primary, Secondary and/or TVET.\r\nExperience in boarding school management is an added advantage.\r\nDemonstrated success in leading organizational change and school transformation', 'Core Competencies\r\n\r\nThe successful candidate should demonstrate:\r\n\r\nStrategic and visionary leadership.\r\nInstructional leadership.\r\nChange management and innovation.\r\nFinancial management and business development.\r\nStakeholder engagement and partnership building.\r\nTeam leadership and performance management.\r\nCompetency-Based Curriculum implementation.\r\nSchool quality assurance and inspection readiness.\r\nEducational data analysis.\r\nChild safeguarding and protection.\r\nTVET program management.\r\nBudgeting and resource management.\r\nEnglish language development.\r\nStrong communication, integrity, accountability and professionalism.\r\nPerformance Expectations\r\n\r\nThe successful candidate will be expected to deliver measurable annual results, including:\r\n\r\nImproved learner achievement and national examination performance.\r\nSchool-wide English language transformation.\r\nGrowth in student enrolment and retention.\r\nExpansion of market-driven TVET programs and industry partnerships.\r\nAt least 20% annual growth in school-generated revenue through enrolment growth, program expansion, approved income-generating initiatives and strategic partnerships.\r\nReduced operational costs through efficient resource utilization.\r\nHigh compliance with NESA inspection standards and safeguarding requirements.\r\nEnhanced stakeholder satisfaction and school reputation.', 'Fixed-Term', 'Interested candidates should submit:\r\nAn application letter;\r\nA detailed Curriculum Vitae;\r\nCopies of academic and professional certificates;\r\nThree (3) traceable professional references.\r\nApplications should be sent to sos.recruitment@sos-rwanda.org .\r\nPlease indicate \"Application for School Principal – SOS Kayonza School\" in the subject line of your email. Female candidates are strongly encouraged to apply, and only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.\r\nChild Safeguarding Statement\r\nSOS Children\'s Villages Rwanda and Impactful Solutions Rwanda (ISR-CBC) are committed to safeguarding children and maintaining a zero-tolerance policy against sexual exploitation, abuse, harassment and all forms of misconduct. Recruitment decisions include rigorous background checks, police clearance, reference verification and assessment of candidates\' commitment to child safeguarding and the organization\'s values.\r\nDone at Kigali on 22nd July 2026\r\nGeorge Gakuba\r\nManaging Director', '', 'sos.recruitment@sos-rwanda.org', 'Eastern', 'Kayonza', 'kayonza', 'Full-time', '3–5 years of progressive educational leadership ex', 'bachelor’s degree in education or master’s degree in educational leadership', 'RWF', 'monthly', '2026-08-02', 1, 'published', 91, 0, 1, '2026-07-22 18:52:29', '2026-07-29 14:58:20', NULL);
INSERT INTO `jobs` (`id`, `company_id`, `company_name`, `company_logo`, `category_id`, `title`, `slug`, `description`, `responsibilities`, `requirements`, `qualifications`, `benefits`, `how_to_apply`, `application_url`, `application_email`, `province`, `district`, `location`, `employment_type`, `experience_level`, `education_level`, `salary_currency`, `salary_period`, `application_deadline`, `is_featured`, `status`, `views`, `applications_count`, `is_active`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(25, NULL, 'RWANDA STANDARD BOARD (RSB)', 'logos/img_6a637c4d9dd25.png', 20, 'LABORATORY ATTENDANT', 'laboratory-attendant', 'The Rwanda Standards Board (RSB) is the public national standards body established by the Government of Rwanda to develop, publish, and promote national standards, metrology services, and conformity assessments. Formed in 2002, the agency operates as a specialized service provider to improve the competitiveness of Rwandan products and ensure consumer protection', '1. Maintaining, monitoring, and recording the performance of the autoclave used for\r\ndecontamination.\r\n2. Compiling and keeping together the records of Lab-ware.\r\n3. Collecting and transferring used lab ware to the wash-up room from designated places\r\nof various laboratories.\r\n4. Decontamination of microbiology lab ware and wastes.\r\n5. Cleaning of glassware and laboratory coats.\r\n6. Reporting broken glassware for replacement.\r\n7. Identifying and requisitioning controlled document laboratory cleaning consumables.\r\n8. Issuing clean glassware to laboratory analysts.\r\n9. Keeping the washroom clean and well organized.', 'Diploma (A2) in Chemistry\r\n Diploma (A2) in Biology\r\n Diploma (A2) in related combinations of Biology and Chemistry\r\n Diploma (A2) in Medical Laboratory', 'Resources management skills\r\nFluency in English, Kinyarwanda and/or French. Knowledge of all is an added advantage\r\nTime management skills\r\nRisk management skills\r\nResults oriented\r\nDigital literacy skills', '', 'Interested and Qualified candidates can apply by clicking on the apply link', 'https://recruitment.mifotra.gov.rw', '', 'Kigali', '', '', 'Full-time', 'beginers', 'A2 DIPLOMA', 'RWF', 'monthly', '2026-07-31', 0, 'published', 138, 0, 1, '2026-07-24 14:53:01', '2026-07-29 13:35:36', NULL),
(26, NULL, 'One Acre Fund', 'logos/img_6a644c4eb70a4.jpg', 17, 'Rwanda Driver ( Fixed-Term)', 'rwanda-driver-fixed-term', 'About One Acre Fund: \r\nFounded in 2006, One Acre Fund equips 5.5 million smallholder farmers to make their farms more productive. Across nine countries that together are home to two-thirds of Africa\'s farmers, we provide high-quality farm supplies, tree seedlings, accessible credit, modern agronomic training, and a wide range of other agricultural services. On average, this model enables any farmer to increase their income and assets on supported land by more than 35 percent, while permanently improving their resilience. This is all made possible by our team of 9,000+ full-time staff, drawn from diverse backgrounds and professions. To learn more, please see our Why Work Here blog post.\r\nOur Rwanda program, founded in 2007 is our largest and operates under the local brand Tubura. We have more than 3,000 staff across all four provinces of Rwanda, as well as in Kigali. Together, we served more than 2.8 million farmers in 2024. We work closely with the government to support national efforts to improve food security. Additionally, we help channel funding and resources to promising agri-SMEs, supporting farmers by providing a market for high-impact crops such as coffee, avocado, and chili.\r\n\r\nAbout the Role:\r\nSeeking a professional driver with a valid driving license and 3+ years of experience in a fast-paced organization. Demonstrates safe driving, vehicle care, reliability, professionalism, strong communication skills, and commitment to safety.', 'Safely Transport Staff & Materials\r\n\r\nSafely transport staff to meetings, field visits, and other work-related activities.\r\nDeliver materials, equipment, and supplies to assigned locations on time.\r\nFollow all road safety regulations and company driving policies at all times.\r\nCoordinate Daily Transport Activities\r\n\r\nPlan and organize daily vehicle movements based on transport requests.\r\nCommunicate with staff to ensure timely pickups, drop-offs, and deliveries.\r\nCoordinate vehicle availability with other teams when required.\r\nMaintain Company Vehicles\r\n\r\nKeep the assigned vehicle clean, safe, and in good working condition.\r\nPerform routine vehicle inspections and report any faults or maintenance needs promptly.\r\nEnsure the vehicle always has the required documents, safety equipment, and basic supplies.\r\nMaintain Accurate Records\r\n\r\nKeep vehicle logbooks, fuel records, and maintenance records up to date.\r\nSubmit required transport and fuel documentation on time.\r\nReport any accidents or incidents according to company procedures.\r\nSupport Safe & Professional Operations\r\n\r\nRepresent the organization professionally when interacting with staff, partners, and community members.\r\nSafeguard company vehicles and equipment and ensure they are used responsibly.\r\nSupport other transport-related duties as assigned.\r\nCareer Growth and Development\r\n\r\nWe have a strong culture of constant learning and we invest in developing our people. You’ll have weekly check-ins with your manager, access to mentorship and training programs, and regular feedback on your performance. We hold career reviews every six months, and set aside time to discuss your aspirations and career goals. You’ll have the opportunity to shape a growing organization and build a rewarding long-term career.', '', 'Across all roles, these are the general qualifications we look for. For this role specifically, you will have:\r\n\r\nA valid Rwanda driver\'s license (Category B and D).\r\nAt least 3 years of experience in the same capacity within a fast-paced environment.\r\nGood knowledge of Rwanda\'s road network and traffic regulations. Safe driving record and commitment to road safety.\r\nBasic knowledge of vehicle maintenance and the ability to identify mechanical issues.\r\nAbility to keep accurate vehicle maintenance, fuel records, and basic computer skills.\r\nWillingness to travel regularly and work in different locations across Rwanda.\r\nAbility to use Google Workspace (Google Sheet & Google Form, etc).\r\nFluent in Kinyarwanda; ability to speak and write in English.', 'Health insurance, paid time off', 'One Acre Fund never asks candidates to pay any money or pay for tests at any stage of the interview process. Official One Acre Fund emails will always arrive from an @oneacrefund.org address. Please report any suspicious communication here (globalhotline@oneacrefund.org), but do not send applications or application materials to this email address.\r\n\r\nDiversity, Equity, Inclusion (DEI), and anti-racism are deeply connected to our organization’s mission and purpose. One Acre Fund aspires to build a culture where all staff feel consistently valued, represented, and connected – so that our team can thrive as professionals, and achieve exceptional impact for the farmers we serve.\r\n\r\nWe are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability, gender, gender identity or expression. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace.', 'https://grnh.se/9kdzwwa21us', '', 'Kigali', 'Rubengera', 'Rubengera', 'Full-time', '3 YEARS OF EXPERIENCE', '', 'RWF', 'monthly', '2026-07-31', 1, 'published', 288, 0, 1, '2026-07-25 05:40:30', '2026-07-30 05:21:35', NULL),
(27, NULL, 'Blackbuck Coffee Ltd', 'logos/img_6a6484629e4f5.jpg', 13, 'Sales Assistant', 'sales-assistant', 'Blackbuck Coffee Ltd is a Rwandan-based company specialized in the coffee industry, delivering high-quality coffee machines and grinders to businesses such as cafes, hotels, and offices. The machines are available for sale or rent. In addition to the premium equipment, Blackbuck Coffee Ltd provides many spare parts for coffee machines (+1000 references) and freshly roasted coffee beans.\r\n\"Blackbuck has equipped Rwanda\'s best cafés, hotels, and offices with professional espresso machines, grinders, and technical service since 2020. We\'re looking for a Sales Assistant to assist our Sales Manager. Blackbuck\'s main office is in Kigali, Gikondo.\r\n\r\nThe role: \r\nYou\'ll assist the sales manager to sell professional coffee machines (both sales and rentals), advise customers based on their needs, and manage the process from first contact through to delivery. The work is split between our showroom and the field, meeting cafés, hotels, and businesses nationwide.\r\n', 'a. Welcome and advise customers in the showroom\r\nb. Prospect and build a portfolio of professional clients\r\nc. Negotiate and close sales and rentals\r\nd. Follow up with customers and coordinate deliveries with the technical team', '', 'What we\'re looking for\r\n\r\na. Fluent French or English required\r\nb. Able to use a computer (email, basic spreadsheets)\r\nc. Comfortable talking to customers\r\nd. Independent, organized, and reliable\r\ne. Willingness to learn the product', '', 'How to Apply\r\nIf you’re ready to join us and contribute to Rwanda’s coffee industry, please submit your CV to their Email jobs@blackbuck.rw. Mention “Sales Assistant Application\" the subject line. We look forward to hearing from you!\r\n\r\nfor more information on our products and service please visit\r\nblackbuck.rw\"', '', 'jobs@blackbuck.rw', 'Kigali', 'kigali', 'Kigali', 'Full-time', '', 'A2 DIPLOMA', 'RWF', 'monthly', '2026-08-21', 1, 'published', 13, 0, 1, '2026-07-25 09:39:46', '2026-07-29 16:20:39', NULL),
(28, NULL, 'Reality Vacation Innovations', 'logos/img_6a64868a1beec.png', 13, 'Tele marketers', 'tele-marketers', 'RVI Destinations a whole new way of discovering the world. Whether you’re looking for a once in a lifetime holiday or just a relaxing getaway at any one of our superior leisure destinations, RVI Destinations can take you there – simply, flexibly, and in style.\r\nINTERNATIONAL COMPANY\r\nFantastic opportunity available in a Leading international sales and marketing company in the Leisure Industry with offices in South Africa, Ivory Coast, Ghana, Nigeria, Cameroon & Angola their exciting new product here in Kigali for the very first time.', 'Educating prospects on our product.\r\nBuilding rapport with customers.\r\nTracking customer’s preferences metrics and media campaigns.\r\nRepresenting the company at launches events and trade shows.\r\nBrain storming ideas and participating in training and workshops\r\nMaintaining a positive image of the brand at all times.', 'ALL APPLICANTS HAVE TO BE FLUENT IN ENGLISH!\r\nSuccessful candidates will be given full in-house training.\r\nMarket-related salaries and good commissions\r\nOpportunity for growth within the company', 'Diploma or Bachelor’s Degree in related field\r\nFluent in Both French and English.\r\nPrior experience in a customer related environment.\r\nFriendly approachable and outgoing.\r\nWorking knowledge of social media platform tools.\r\nAbility to travel.\r\nPassport Picture\r\nSuccessful candidates must be well spoken and be outgoing with good people skills.\r\nCandidates must be 23 Years and above.', '', 'Applicants are to forward CV’s to jobs.rvikigali@gmail.com', '', 'jobs.rvikigali@gmail.com', 'Kigali', 'KIGALI', '', 'Full-time', 'Entry level (1 to 3 years of experience)', 'Bachelor', 'RWF', 'monthly', '2026-08-23', 1, 'published', 27, 0, 1, '2026-07-25 09:48:58', '2026-07-30 03:10:06', NULL),
(29, NULL, 'Wicloud', 'logos/img_6a6488f453385.jpg', 20, 'Recruiter', 'recruiter', 'We are, Wicloud, established in mid-2022, with over 1000 employees across 3 offices in the international. Wicloud dedicates the One-Stop Digital Transformation Service to our customers. Renowned for delivering premium IT outsourcing services exclusively \r\ntailored for Microsoft clients for 4 products: Microsoft Dynamics 365, Microsoft Azure, Microsoft Windows Commercial, and Microsoft Office 365.', 'Initiate outbound communications to source prospective candidates for software engineering and other technical roles at varying skill levels \r\nCollaborate with hiring managers to create accurate and complete job descriptions and hiring criteria \r\nCollaborate with hiring managers, People team members, and executives on the offer process, defining salary ranges, incentives, start dates, and other pertinent details\r\nConduct phone screens, interviews, and schedule steps in the application process\r\nUsing relevant recruiting metrics like time-to-fill and candidate assessment data, evaluate and refine current processes \r\nEstablishing a playbook for recruiting to take our talent acquisition methods to the next level ', 'Possess no less than 5 years of professional recruitment experience; \r\nBe proficient in utilizing local mainstream recruitment channels in Kigali for talent hunting; \r\nAble to use English as daily working language proficiently for all recruitment-related communication; \r\nHave solid connections and in-depth knowledge of talent resources from local universities in Kigali; \r\nFamiliar with local labor laws and relevant employment regulatory provisions of Rwanda.', '', 'Play a key role in attracting and building high-performing teams that contribute to the company\'s success. \r\nGain valuable professional experience while working closely with leadership and cross-functional teams. \r\nEnjoy opportunities for career growth, learning, and professional development. \r\nReceive competitive compensation, full support during onboarding, and the tools needed to succeed. ', 'All interested candidates should send their CVs and cover letters to their Email ', '', 'francis@itechwx.com', 'Kigali', 'KIGALI', '', 'Full-time', '5 years of experience', 'Bachelor&#039;s Degree', 'RWF', 'monthly', '2026-07-31', 1, 'published', 45, 0, 1, '2026-07-25 09:59:16', '2026-07-29 16:21:12', NULL);
INSERT INTO `jobs` (`id`, `company_id`, `company_name`, `company_logo`, `category_id`, `title`, `slug`, `description`, `responsibilities`, `requirements`, `qualifications`, `benefits`, `how_to_apply`, `application_url`, `application_email`, `province`, `district`, `location`, `employment_type`, `experience_level`, `education_level`, `salary_currency`, `salary_period`, `application_deadline`, `is_featured`, `status`, `views`, `applications_count`, `is_active`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(30, NULL, 'The Dian Fossey Gorilla Fund International', 'logos/img_6a68e223dcb1a.jpg', 9, 'Conservation Gallery Assistant', 'conservation-gallery-assistant', 'About the Dian Fossey Gorilla Fund\r\n\r\nThe Dian Fossey Gorilla Fund is the world’s largest and longest-running organisation dedicated to gorilla conservation. As a global nongovernmental organization, we work with the Government of Rwanda, scientists, local communities, and conservation partners to conduct conservation programs that enable gorillas and people to thrive together.\r\n\r\nThe heart of our operations in Rwanda is the Ellen DeGeneres Campus of the Dian Fossey Gorilla Fund in Kinigi. From the Campus, we support the daily protection and scientific study of gorillas and their habitat, train future conservation leaders, and implement programs that support surrounding communities.\r\n\r\nAs part of our education and public engagement activities, the campus includes a Conservation Gallery which welcomes visitors from Rwanda and around the world.\r\n\r\nAbout the candidate\r\n\r\nWe are seeking an enthusiastic, confident, and motivated candidate to join the Conservation Gallery team and support the delivery of high-quality visitor experiences.\r\n\r\nWe are looking for someone who is comfortable interacting with people, while also being professional, reliable, and eager to learn about gorillas, conservation, and the work of the Dian Fossey Gorilla Fund.\r\n\r\nThis position may be suitable as a first professional career opportunity for a recent graduate or someone who has gained relevant experience through an internship, volunteering, tourism activities, customer service, or visitor engagement.\r\n\r\nThe position offers the opportunity to work with an experienced team, interact with visitors from Rwanda and around the world, and develop valuable professional skills within one of the world’s leading gorilla conservation organizations.\r\n\r\nJob title: Conservation Gallery Assistant\r\n\r\nDuty station: Ellen DeGeneres Campus of the Dian Fossey Gorilla Fund, Kinigi, Rwanda\r\n\r\nPosition type: Full-time\r\n\r\nReports to: Visitor Experience and Hospitality Manager\r\n\r\nJob summary\r\n\r\nThe Conservation Gallery Assistant will be a key member of the Gallery team and will help ensure the efficient and successful delivery of visitor experience and hospitality activities.\r\n\r\nWorking closely with the Visitor Experience and Hospitality Manager and the wider Gallery team, the Gallery Assistant will support daily operations, welcome and register visitors, process payments and donations, monitor exhibitions and interactive devices, and assist visitors throughout their experience.\r\n\r\nA major responsibility of this position will be delivering engaging guided tours, including behind the scenes tours, school visits, and special visitor experiences such as private events and sundowners. Formal training is provided before leading the tours.\r\n\r\nThe successful candidate must therefore be confident in public speaking and able to communicate information in a clear, accurate, and engaging way. The role requires regular interaction with visitors from different countries, cultures, backgrounds, and age groups.', 'Welcome visitors to the Campus in a warm, professional, and organized manner.\r\nManage visitor registration, payments, and donation procedures.\r\nCollect all required visitor information and maintain accurate visitor records and support data entry and visitor information management.\r\nProvide visitors with clear information about the Conservation Gallery, the Dian Fossey Gorilla Fund, and the different visitor experiences available.\r\nDeliver engaging guided tours for general visitors, school groups, VIP guests, donors, partners, and other special visitors.\r\nAssist with the coordination and delivery of VIP experiences, guided tours, sundowners, private events, and other special activities.\r\nSupport visitors throughout their visit by answering questions, explaining exhibitions, and assisting with the use of interactive devices.\r\nHelp maintain a high standard of customer service throughout the entire visitor experience.\r\nMonitor the Gallery’s exhibitions, devices, equipment, and overall appearance to ensure that everything is clean, organized, and functioning properly.\r\nSupport basic troubleshooting of the 360 degree theater, Virtual Reality, Augmented Reality, tablets, and other interactive devices, in collaboration with the relevant technical teams and report all of the technical problems and resolution to the Manager.\r\nPerform Gallery opening and closing procedures according to established standards.\r\nParticipate in the rotation of Gallery staff across different visitor stations and responsibilities.\r\nSupport the orientation, training, and supervision of interns, students, and new team members working in the Gallery.\r\nParticipate in training sessions, workshops, and professional development activities organized by the Dian Fossey Gorilla Fund.\r\nPrepare and submit a weekly report summarizing completed activities, visitor experiences, challenges, and follow-up actions.\r\nWork collaboratively with Gallery colleagues and other departments to ensure that visitors receive a well organized, welcoming, and memorable experience.\r\nPerform other duties related to the position as assigned.', 'Bachelor’s degree in tourism, hospitality, communication, education, conservation or another relevant field.\r\nHaving a minimum of 1 year of experience in tourism, hospitality, customer service, guiding, education, or visitor engagement is an advantage. This experience may have been gained through employment, an internship, volunteering, school activities, or community involvement.\r\nStrong spoken and written English and Kinyarwanda. Knowledge of French or another international language is an advantage.\r\nConfidence in public speaking and the ability to deliver engaging presentations and guided tours to different audiences.\r\nGood computer skills, including email, internet use, Google Docs, spreadsheets, data entry, and basic database management.p\r\nA genuine interest in conservation.\r\nStrong organizational skills and the ability to manage several responsibilities during busy visitor periods.\r\nGood problem-solving skills and the ability to respond calmly and professionally to unexpected situations.\r\nAbility to work effectively with colleagues from different teams, professional backgrounds, and different nationalities. ', '', '', 'Interested candidates are requested to submit their resume (no longer than 2 pages) and a cover letter outlining work experience, achievements and career ambition via email\r\nThe Fossey Fund is an equal-opportunity employer, and all qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted for interviews.\r\nFor more information about our work, please visit:www.gorillafund.org\r\nApplication Deadline: 14th August 2026 at 5:00 pm.\r\nDone at Kinigi, on 28th July 2026.\r\nFelix Ndagijimana\r\nDirector, Rwanda Programs.', '', 'karisokejobs@gorillafund.org', 'Kigali', '', 'KIGALI', 'Full-time', 'Entry level (1 to 3 years of experience)', 'Bachelor&#039;s Degree', 'RWF', 'monthly', '2026-08-14', 1, 'published', 5, 0, 1, '2026-07-28 17:08:51', '2026-07-29 16:26:09', NULL),
(31, NULL, 'BIRUNGA SACCO MUSANZE (BSM)', 'logos/img_6a68e4891d48f.png', 3, 'Teller', 'teller-1785259145', 'BIRUNGA SACCO MUSANZE is a District Savings and Credit Cooperative (D-SACCO) established following the consolidation of 15 U-SACCOs operating within MUSANZE District, in accordance with the Government of Rwanda SACCO\'s consolidation framework. \r\nBIRUNGA SACCO MUSANZE is looking for qualified, competent, committed, proactive and self-motivated individual to occupy the following positions at Head office and Branch level:\r\nPosition: TELLER\r\nNumber: 4', 'Under the supervision and guidance of the Branch Operations Officer/Outlet responsible, the Teller has the following main responsibilities: \r\n\r\nTo work diligently on the assigned work on time and to produce results;\r\n To comply with the instructions of the employer or his/her representative;\r\nTo take good care of and manage the equipment assigned to him/her in his/her work;\r\nTo be at work and respect working days and hours;\r\nTo maintain the confidentiality of work;\r\n To provide basic identification documents before starting work;\r\nTo follow the principles and codes of conduct governing the business activities of the Cooperative;\r\nConducts cash related services to customers/ members, e.g., withdrawals and deposits;\r\nInitiates transfers from customer/member accounts, e.g., interbranch transfer;\r\nPerforms cheques related services to customers/ members, e.g., crediting a cheque;\r\nPerforms disbursements of loans;\r\nPerforms change of coinage and foreign exchanges;\r\nSupports in opening, filling, discharging, and closing a till;\r\nPerforms cross-selling;\r\nTo welcome and assist members who need services related to deposits and withdrawals;\r\nTo receive and pay members or customers the approved amount;\r\nTo manage the till/store he/she is responsible for;\r\nTo fill out the member\'s booklet correctly;\r\nParticipate in the closing of the daily operations of the Cooperative, especially the control of funds;\r\nProvide all documents supporting his/her daily operations;\r\nBe held accountable for all errors that appear in his daily operations, including the shortage or excess/ surplus of funds;\r\nPerform other duties that do not conflict with the laws and regulations required by the supervisor or his/her superior authority.', 'At least secondary education (A2) in related domain;\r\nBasic IT literacy of CBS and Office;\r\nAbility to handle transactions accurately and responsibly;\r\nGood math skills;\r\nAttention to detail;\r\nCustomer satisfaction oriented.', 'Motivation letter (addressed to the Chairperson of the Board of Directors);\r\nUpdated CV; \r\nCopies of academic degrees or professional certificate;\r\nCopy of National ID;\r\nProof of experience;\r\nAny other relevant supporting documents to prove experience and skills.', '', 'Submission Guidelines: \r\nAll interested and qualified candidates are invited to submit their applications comprising all mentioned documents to BIRUNGA SACCO MUSANZE Head Office not later than 04th August 2026 at 16 :00 pm .', '', '', 'Southern', 'MUSANZE', 'MUSANZE', 'Full-time', 'Entry level (1 to 3 years of experience)', 'A2 DIPLOMA', 'RWF', 'monthly', '2026-08-04', 0, 'published', 1, 0, 1, '2026-07-28 17:19:04', '2026-07-29 11:41:21', NULL);
INSERT INTO `jobs` (`id`, `company_id`, `company_name`, `company_logo`, `category_id`, `title`, `slug`, `description`, `responsibilities`, `requirements`, `qualifications`, `benefits`, `how_to_apply`, `application_url`, `application_email`, `province`, `district`, `location`, `employment_type`, `experience_level`, `education_level`, `salary_currency`, `salary_period`, `application_deadline`, `is_featured`, `status`, `views`, `applications_count`, `is_active`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES
(32, NULL, 'Catholic Relief Services (CRS)', 'logos/img_6a68e7c1d90f8.jpg', 20, 'Youth Development &amp; Livelihoods - Program Manager', 'youth-development-amp-livelihoods-program-manager', 'Catholic Relief Services is the official international humanitarian agency of the Catholic community in the United States. CRS works to save, protect, and transform lives in need in more than 100 countries, without regard to race, religion or nationality. CRS’ relief and development work is accomplished through programs of emergency response, HIV, health, agriculture, education, microfinance and peacebuilding. \r\n\r\nJob Summary\r\n\r\nYou will manage CRS Rwanda\'s youth economic development and livelihoods programming, including projects that promote youth entrepreneurship, employment pathways, access to finance, enterprise development, and rural livelihoods. You will manage all activities throughout the project cycle and provide technical and operational oversight to project staff and implementing partners. You will also coordinate project-level engagement with government technical counterparts, implementing partners, private sector actors, financial service providers, and youth-serving organizations. Your management skills, technical knowledge, and understanding of market-oriented youth programming will ensure that the Country Program delivers high-quality, inclusive programming and continuously works towards improving results for rural and underserved youth. You will provide technical evidence and implementation input to program development, organizational partnerships, and external engagement processes.', 'Manage and implement all activities throughout relevant project cycles - project design, start-up, implementation, monitoring, and close-out - to ensure efficient and effective implementation in line with CRS program quality principles and standards, donor requirements, and good practices. Ensure project teams and partner staff use the appropriate systems and tools.\r\nProvide technical and operational oversight for youth economic development and livelihoods programming, including youth entrepreneurship, employability and employment pathways, access to finance, rural livelihoods integrating life skills, social and emotional wellbeing, positive youth development approaches. Ensure approaches are market-responsive, inclusive, and relevant to the realities of rural and underserved youth.\r\nEffectively manage talent and supervise. Manage team dynamics and staff well-being. Provide coaching, strategically tailor individual development plans, contribute to the recruitment process of project staff, and complete performance management for direct reports.\r\nManage program-level relationships and implementation arrangements with partner organizations. Review and monitor partner workplans, budgets, forecasts, reports, deliverables, and performance; conduct regular review meetings and field visits; and ensure timely follow-up on agreed actions.\r\nChampion learning with project staff and partner teams. Analyze and evaluate project performance data following CRS MEAL policy. Proactively identify issues and concerns, facilitate reflection and adaptive management, and use participatory processes to overcome obstacles to implementation\r\nCoordinate the identification of staff and partner capacity and technical assistance needs and the design and delivery of capacity-strengthening interventions required to support quality project implementation, financial stewardship, reporting, and accountability.\r\nCoordinate and monitor financial, material, and operational resources relevant to project needs. Through work planning, budgeting, forecasting, expenditure monitoring, procurement coordination, and oversight, ensure efficient and accountable use of project resources.\r\nCoordinate technical and project-level engagement with district authorities, relevant government technical units and Ministries, private sector actors, financial institutions, business development service providers, and youth-serving organizations. Represent CRS in relevant technical working groups, project coordination meetings, and implementation forums, as delegated.\r\nAct as a key technical resource person in project design and proposal development in the youth programming area, providing implementation evidence, technical content, realistic delivery arrangements, partner input, workplans, and budgets, and taking on program growth responsibilities as needed.\r\nHelp identify, assess, and strengthen partnerships relevant to youth projects, applying appropriate partnership concepts, tools, and approaches. Coordinate with the Partnerships and Strategic Initiatives Manager and Country Manager on opportunities requiring organizational-level partnership development, business development, strategic positioning, or high-level engagement.', 'Strong project cycle management skills, including work planning, budgeting, forecasting, risk management, partner oversight, reporting, and coordination of operational requirements.\r\nDemonstrated project management depth combined with a broad understanding of youth economic empowerment, private sector engagement, financial inclusion, and rural programming.\r\nGood understanding of the opportunities and constraints affecting rural and underserved youth and the importance of linking youth programming to viable markets, employers, finance, and enterprise support services.\r\nExperience using MS Windows and MS Office packages (Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Outlook), Web Conferencing Applications, and information management systems.\r\nExperience engaging with and managing partner organizations, including reviewing workplans, budgets, reports, and performance and supporting partner capacity strengthening.\r\nExperience in technical-level engagement with government institutions, private sector actors, financial service providers, and youth-serving organizations.\r\nExperience contributing to the development of technical proposals, concept notes, project budgets, and implementation arrangements.\r\nStrong analytical, critical thinking, and creative problem-solving skills with the ability to make sound judgment and use program and financial data to inform decisions.\r\nStrong relationship management, facilitation, and negotiation skills\r\nStrong written and verbal communication skills with the ability to prepare clear reports, presentations, and technical documents.\r\nProactive, agile, results-oriented, service-oriented, and able to learn new technical areas, systems, and processes quickly.\r\nRequired Languages: Excellent written and spoken English and Kinyarwanda required. Knowledge of French is desirable.\r\nTravel: Must be willing and able to travel up to 40% within Rwanda, including rural project locations.\r\nSupervisory Responsibilities: Yes - Youth Policy and Partnerships Advisor and Youth Digital Programming Officer.\r\nCRS is an equal opportunity employer. Applications from women and youth are highly welcomed.', 'Master\'s Degree in a relevant field.\r\nExperience in two or more of the following areas: youth entrepreneurship, employment and workforce development, access to finance, enterprise development, rural livelihoods, or market systems development.\r\nExperience engaging private sector actors, employers, financial institutions, or business development service providers in support of youth programming.\r\nExperience working with rural youth and applying inclusive approaches for young women, youth with disabilities, and other underserved groups.\r\nMEAL, adaptive management, program learning skills and experience preferred. ', '', 'Interested and qualified candidates should Fill out form: https://forms.office.com/r/1SCfA52cbm  the Self -DeclarationClause and submit them together with one page Cover letter plus updated CV (maximum three pages) all in/as one PDF document - via email only \r\nAlso include your full names and title “Youth Program Manager I in the subject line. Due to anticipated high interest in this post and the expected number of applicants, only short-listed candidates will be contacted.\r\n\r\nPlease, include the statement below in your cover letter: “By applying to this job, I understand and acknowledge that CRS requires its staff to treat all people with dignity and respect and to actively prevent harassment, abuse, exploitation, and human trafficking. Further, I understand that if I am a successful candidate, I will be subject to a comprehensive background check, and my personal/professional references will be asked to evaluate my behaviors related to the above safeguarding-related topics.”', 'https://forms.office.com/r/1SCfA52cbm', 'RW_HR@crs.org', 'Kigali', '', 'KIGALI', 'Full-time', 'Senior (5+ years of experience)', 'Bachelor&#039;s Degree', 'RWF', 'monthly', '2026-08-04', 1, 'published', 3, 0, 1, '2026-07-28 17:32:49', '2026-07-29 09:22:41', NULL),
(33, NULL, 'YELLOW AFRICA', 'logos/img_6a69be0b12c74.png', 13, 'Independent Field Rep', 'independent-field-rep', 'Yellow is an African company that provides digital financial services and access to essential products, especially through a network of local agents. In Rwanda, Yellow has operated with a model where field representatives/agents help customers access products and services.\r\nSome key things about Yellow Africa Rwanda:\r\nField Representatives (YRR / Retail Sales Representatives): Independent sales agents who sell products, support customers, and grow the Yellow network.\r\nPhone financing model: Agents can provide smartphones to customers through a payment plan, often using a device-locking system until payments are completed.\r\nWorking capital approach: Agents may receive products or business support to sell and generate income.\r\nCollateral system: Used to reduce risk when providing phones or business resources.\r\nDigital inclusion goal: Helping more people access smartphones and digital services.', 'Find and Acquire Customers\r\nIdentify potential customers who need smartphones.\r\nExplain Yellow’s phone financing plans.\r\nRegister customers and help them get suitable devices.\r\nSell Smartphones\r\nPromote and sell Yellow phones in your assigned area.\r\nAchieve sales targets by increasing the number of customers.\r\nCustomer Support\r\nGuide customers on payment schedules.\r\nFollow up with customers to ensure they make payments on time.\r\nProvide basic support after selling phones.\r\nManage Stock and Devices\r\nTake responsibility for phones provided by Yellow.\r\nKeep phones safe before they are sold.\r\nTrack stock using the Yellow Digital Wallet system.\r\nUse Yellow Digital Wallet\r\nManage inventory.\r\nMonitor sales and commissions.\r\nTrack business growth and earnings.\r\nMarket Expansion\r\nBuild relationships with customers and communities.\r\nFind new opportunities to increase sales.\r\nGrow your customer portfolio.\r\nMaintain Good Customer Relationships\r\nBe honest and professional with customers.\r\nEnsure customers understand the payment process and terms.', 'Valid National ID\r\nSecondary education or equivalent\r\nSmartphone and digital skills\r\nGood communication and sales skills\r\nCustomer service ability\r\nAbility to work in the field independently\r\nSales/marketing experience is an advantage\r\nEntrepreneurial mindset and commitment to targets', 'Secondary school certificate (O’Level) or higher\r\nExperience in sales, marketing, or customer service (advantage)\r\nGood communication and negotiation skills\r\nBasic smartphone and digital skills\r\nAbility to work independently and meet targets\r\nCustomer relationship management skills\r\nBusiness/entrepreneurial mindset', 'Earn commissions from successful sales\r\nOpportunity to grow your own business\r\nAccess to smartphone sales opportunities\r\nFlexible working schedule\r\nGain sales and entrepreneurship experience\r\nBuild customer and business networks\r\nTraining and support from Yellow Africa\r\nOpportunity for income growth based on performance', 'Interested candidates can contact us on WhatsApp at +250780092252.', 'https://kulahire.yellow.africa/candidate/register?ref=2E3X&amp;amp;role=field-rep&amp;amp;country=Rwanda', '', '', '', 'kayonza,rusizi,huye,rwamagana,muhanga,musanze', 'Freelance', 'Entry level (1 to 3 years of experience)', '', 'RWF', 'monthly', '2026-08-31', 1, 'published', 227, 0, 1, '2026-07-29 08:47:07', '2026-07-30 05:28:40', NULL);

